<title>USA: NRC delays okay Wash. 1,112 MW nuclear unit start.</title>
<headline>NRC delays okay Wash. 1,112 MW nuclear unit start.</headline>
<dateline>LOS ANGELES 1997-06-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>Nuclear Regulatory Commission (NRC) approval for restart of the 1,112 megawatt (MW) WNP-2 nuclear power plant in Washington state will not be received before Thursday, a spokesman for the plant said Monday.</p>
<p>The NRC is still evaluating an amendment of technical specifications for the plant, he noted.</p>
<p>If word from the NRC comes Thursday, the unit would be restarted, but would not complete its outage until testing is finished, likely on Monday July 7, the spokesman added.</p>
<p>WNP-2 has been shut since late March.</p>
<p>((--Los Angeles bureau + 1 213 955 6761))</p>
